That is, when $T\gg 0$, our algorithm not only stabilizes the system so that $\frac 1T \operatornamewithlimits{\mathbb{E}}\left [\sum_{t=1}^T \lVert Q(t)\rVert_1\right ]=\operatorname{\mathcal O}_T(1)$, but also enjoys an average utility approaching that of the reference policy polynomially fast, \textit{i.e.}, $\frac 1T \operatornamewithlimits{\mathbb{E}}\left [\sum_{t=1}^T \left (g_{t}(\mathring{\lambda}(t)) - g_{t}(\lambda(t))\right )\right ]=\operatorname{\mathcal O}_T(V^{-1})$ -- the utility maximization objective 3 is ensured.
